# Files excluded from Vercel deployments.
#
# Without this file the CLI uploads the whole working directory, which on a
# developer machine includes .env, the local SQLite database and the venv.
# Keeping this list aligned with .gitignore means a CLI deploy and a
# Git-triggered deploy send the same tree, so the two cannot drift.

# Secrets — never ship these into a function bundle
.env
.env.*
data_dump.json

# Local database
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal

# Local virtualenvs (dependencies are installed from requirements.txt)
venv/
env/
.venv/

# Build output. Deliberately excluded: staticfiles/ is gitignored, so a
# Git deploy never has it. Shipping it only from CLI deploys would make
# asset URLs hashed one way and unhashed the other. WhiteNoise serves the
# committed static/ directory directly via WHITENOISE_USE_FINDERS.
staticfiles/
static_collected/

# Caches and local noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.git/
.github/
media/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
